<title>BELGIUM: Commission clears CLT/Bertelsmann merger - EU source.</title>
<headline>Commission clears CLT/Bertelsmann merger - EU source.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commission cleared on Monday the merger between Luxembourg-based broadcaster CLT, which is controllled by Audiofina, and Bertelsmann's television unit UFA, an EU source said.</p>
<p>The source said the Commission had concluded that the operation would not lead to the creation of a dominant position, not even in Germany where the two partners are both active.</p>
<p>This was because they would face competition from commercial television channels linked to rival group operated by Bavarian media mogul Leo Kirch, the source added.</p>
<p>An official statement is expected later on Monday or possibly Tuesday.</p>
<p>Under the terms of the agreement, CLT and UFA will be merged in a joint venture which will be jointly controlled by Bertelsmann and Audiofina.</p>
</text>
